{
  "requirement": "Finishing a verification includes every successful tracked node read in its\n`Fingerprinted`, whether ordinary code or a model tool requested it. Each observation\ncontains the node identity and the fingerprint of the contents actually supplied.\n\nA failed read returns an error without inventing a successful observation.\nRepeating an identical observation adds no information. Reading the same\nidentity with two different fingerprints preserves both observations.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Obligations in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.node_inputs`, and the marked tests that cover each:\n\n1. **Finishing includes every successful tracked read, whether ordinary code or a model tool requested it.**\n   - `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` reads directly with `read` and `read_snapshot`. It asserts that `finish` returns a record whose `dependencies` equal the observed list.\n   - `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace]` mixes direct reads with reads made through `ask().contents_of_current_node()`. It asserts the retained order and that `finish` returns the same list.\n   - `agent/tests.rs#fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` has the `read_node` tool read node 2. It asserts a `Dependency::Node(Node(2), fingerprint)` entry and that `record.dependencies == observations`.\n   - `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]` and `tests/contracts.rs#fn[changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another]` check this through `verify`, `store_evidence` and `load_evidence`. The stored dependencies equal the node reads.\n\n2. **Each observation holds the node identity and the fingerprint of the contents actually supplied.**\n   - `direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots` checks fingerprints for empty and large multi-byte contents. It also checks that the observation is unchanged after the node is replaced.\n   - `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` has the node change after the read and while paging. It asserts the fingerprint value equals the original contents.\n   - `cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input` asserts the exact delivered selection as the recorded value, not the current graph contents.\n\n3. **A failed read returns an error and adds no observation.**\n   - Direct path: `snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions` asserts `read(&2).is_err()` and that node 2 is absent from the dependencies. `direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots` asserts `read(&9)` returns `\"missing\"` and that the dependencies stay empty.\n   - Tool path: in `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery`, a `read_node` call whose result is never delivered leaves `dependencies()` empty. The source-read test asserts that a missing selector adds no input, and the unmarked `node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` also checks the error case.\n\n4. **Identical observations add no information, and different fingerprints for one identity are both preserved.**\n   - `snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions` reads node 1 as \"before\" twice, once with `read` and once with `read_snapshot`. It then reads \"after\". The dependencies are exactly `[Node(1, before), Node(1, after)]`, so duplicates are collapsed and both distinct versions are kept in order.\n   - `earlier` is still `[Node(1, before)]` after the later reads, so a list returned earlier is unchanged by later reads.\n\nI found no scenario in the requirement that a violating implementation could get past these assertions. The tests are marked with `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.node_inputs`.",
